{{Elections in Oklahoma}}
The '''1990 United States Senate election in Oklahoma''' was held November 6, 1990 to elect a member of the [[United States Senate]] to represent the State of [[Oklahoma]] as well as [[United States Senate elections, 1990|other elections]] to the United States Senate in other states and [[United States House of Representatives elections, 1990|elections]] to the [[United States House of Representatives]] and various [[United States elections, 1990#State elections|state]] elections. The primaries were held August 28.

Incumbent Senator [[David Boren]] won re-election to a third term in a landslide over challenger [[Stephen Jones (attorney)|Stephen Jones]], carrying every county in the state with more than 60% of the vote. This is to date the last time Democrats have won a U.S. Senate election in Oklahoma. Boren later resigned his seat in 1994 to become president of the [[University of Oklahoma]].<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-1994-04-28-mn-51532-story.html|title=Boren Will Leave Senate Seat|work=[[Los Angeles Times]]|date=April 28, 1994|access-date=November 4, 2018}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=Senator Inhofe Swearing-in Ceremony {{!}} C-SPAN.org |url=https://www.c-span.org/video/?61651-1/senator-inhofe-swearing-ceremony |access-date=2023-11-12 |website=www.c-span.org}}</ref>

